      {
        "cell": "A36",
        "type": 1,
        "value": "Note to Daily Trends in FPI Investments\n\n* Conversion rate: With effect from January 01, 1999, the daily RBI reference rate as on the trading day has been adopted. (If the trading day is a bank holiday, immediately preceding day's reference rate has been used).\n\nDiscrepancies in total figures, if any, are due to rounding off\n\n\"Note: The data pertains to all the activities undertaken by FPIs in Indian Securities Market, including trades done in secondary market, primary market and activities involved in right/bonus issues, private placement, merger & acquisition, etc.\" \n\nNote:\nThe Stock Exchanges data pertains to following: \nPurchase and sale in secondary market \nPurchase and sale of mutual fund units in secondary market \nPrimary Market and Others data pertains to following: \nPurchase in primary market \nPreferential allotment \nPurchase through rights issue \nConversion of debentures into equity shares \nReceipt of bonus shares \nRedemption of debenture /units of mutual funds \nLodging shares in terms of open offer \nRepurchase of units by mutual fund \nBuyback of shares by company \nPayment of allotment/call money \nSquare off - on account of short delivery received \nSquare off and auction-on account of short delivery given \nConsolidation sub division of securities \n",
        "xf": 112
